<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Bedulu Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">914 CE – 1343 CE (approx.) · capital Bedulu (Pejeng)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Hindu-Buddhist kingdom of Bali under the Warmadewa line, ruling from Bedulu and Pejeng until Majapahit's conquest in 1343.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belanjong-pillar">Belanjong pillar</a> of 914 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanur">Sanur</a> records <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-kesari-warmadewa">Sri Kesari Warmadewa</a>, the first known Balinese king, campaigning on the island. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warmadewa-dynasty">Warmadewa dynasty</a> ruled from the Pejeng and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedulu">Bedulu</a> area, the fertile heart of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ubud">Ubud</a>, for over three centuries.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Royal charters in Old Balinese, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-javanese">Old Javanese</a>, show irrigation communities, ancestors of the subak system, and temples endowed with land. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udayana-warmadewa">Udayana</a> married the Javanese princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahendradatta">Mahendradatta</a>, and their son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/airlangga">Airlangga</a> later ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kahuripan">Kahuripan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. The rock-cut sanctuaries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa-gajah">Goa Gajah</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunung-kawi">Gunung Kawi</a>, the latter linked to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anak-wungsu">Anak Wungsu</a>, date from this period.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1343 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gajah-mada">Gajah Mada</a>, joined according to Balinese tradition by Arya Damar, defeated the last king, remembered as Sri Astasura Ratna Bumi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banten">Banten</a>. Majapahit installed a Javanese dynasty that ruled from Samprangan and then the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gelgel">Kingdom of Gelgel</a>, shaping later Balinese court culture.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bedulu-kingdom.jpg" alt="Bedulu Kingdom" width="320" height="519"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sanur_Belankong_Pillar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>914 CE – 1343 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bedulu (Pejeng)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sri Kesari Warmadewa, Udayana, Anak Wungsu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism and Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Balinese, Old Javanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Bali (Warmadewa), Pejeng, Warmadewa dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1128&amp;focus=bedulu-kingdom" aria-label="Bedulu Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7866 2496 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bedulu Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8186 2752L8114 2731M8186 2752L8112 2721M8186 2752L8189 2753"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8114 2731h0M8112 2721h0M8189 2753h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8186 2752h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8186 2752h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bedulu. <a href="/atlas?year=1128&amp;focus=bedulu-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
